WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.050
I couldn't think of a better way

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:02.900
to end my visit than performing

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:05.510
at Sydney's historic State Theatre.

00:00:05.510 --> 00:00:07.440
I brought along three of my good friends

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.846
from the The Basic Cable Band.

00:00:08.846 --> 00:00:10.800
(crowd cheering and clapping)

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:14.700
Plus, I was joined by three
hilarious Australian comedians.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:18.743
Steen Raskopoulos, Becky
Lucas, and Rhys Nicholson.

00:00:18.743 --> 00:00:19.867
(crowd cheering and applauding)

00:00:19.867 --> 00:00:21.200
Hello Australia!

00:00:22.076 --> 00:00:23.790
(crowd cheering)

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:25.650
You guys, you're so cheerful.

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:26.836
This guy was talking to me he was like,

00:00:26.836 --> 00:00:31.040
yeah, we got no ozone
layer, (crowd laughing)

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:33.470
we got no ozone layer!

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:36.676
And, I thought why is he saying
it like, it's my birthday?

00:00:36.676 --> 00:00:39.820
(crowd laughing)

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:41.368
What's your favorite cereal?
What's the cereal you love?

00:00:41.368 --> 00:00:42.250
(man shouting from crowd)

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:43.597
Wait what?

00:00:43.597 --> 00:00:46.626
This guy out there yelled like
a caveman who'd been shot.

00:00:46.626 --> 00:00:48.810
(crowd laughing)
Duh, bah!

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:51.515
Sir, just that guys who's
been yelling, what is it?

00:00:51.515 --> 00:00:52.845
[Man In Crowd] Weet-Bix!

00:00:52.845 --> 00:00:56.460
(crowd cheering and clapping)

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:58.398
You, come here!

00:00:58.398 --> 00:00:59.394
For (bleep) sake.

00:00:59.394 --> 00:01:03.574
(crowd cheering and laughing)

00:01:03.574 --> 00:01:04.407
What is it again?

00:01:04.407 --> 00:01:06.104
Just you, no one else.

00:01:06.104 --> 00:01:07.013
Weet-Bix.

00:01:07.013 --> 00:01:07.950
Weet-Bix.

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:09.115
And what's it made of?

00:01:09.115 --> 00:01:09.948
Wheat.

00:01:09.948 --> 00:01:13.781
(crowd laughing and clapping)

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:23.662
Should've gone to Melbourne.

00:01:23.662 --> 00:01:25.760
(crowd laughing)

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:28.110
You guys are just screwing
with the rest of the Earth.

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:29.440
(crowd laughing)

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:31.190
I'll 'ave a jubney bubney, what's that?

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:32.490
Cinnamon cracker.

00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:34.350
Wait, well why didn't
you say cinnamon cracker?

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:35.529
(laughing evilly)

00:01:35.529 --> 00:01:36.362
(crowd laughing)

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:37.763
We got 'cha, good on ya.

00:01:39.997 --> 00:01:43.490
Now to be fair, each song
gets an even chance here.

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:48.050
In light blue, You Shook Me
All Night Long by aca-daca.

00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:51.721
And then in yellow,
Skippy the Bush Kangaroo.

00:01:51.721 --> 00:01:55.554
(crowd cheering and clapping)

00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:01.262
Why do you want Skippy the Bush Kangaroo?

00:02:01.262 --> 00:02:04.058
(crowd laughing)

00:02:04.058 --> 00:02:06.858
[Audience Members] Skippy, Skippy!

00:02:06.858 --> 00:02:08.108
Skippy, Skippy!

00:02:09.956 --> 00:02:14.956
(band plays "You Shook Me
All Night Long" by AC/DC)

00:02:17.009 --> 00:02:18.979
♪ She was a fast machine ♪

00:02:18.979 --> 00:02:20.929
♪ She kept her motor clean ♪

00:02:20.929 --> 00:02:25.009
♪ She was the best damn
woman I had ever seen ♪

00:02:25.009 --> 00:02:27.524
♪ 'Cause the walls start shaking ♪

00:02:27.524 --> 00:02:29.374
♪ The earth was quaking ♪

00:02:29.374 --> 00:02:31.338
♪ My mind was aching ♪

00:02:31.338 --> 00:02:34.010
♪ And we were making it and you ♪

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:36.570
Anyone here with the guts to come up here

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:38.735
and try and sing like that?

00:02:38.735 --> 00:02:40.516
♪ I said you ♪

00:02:40.516 --> 00:02:44.016
♪ Shook me all night long ♪

00:02:46.567 --> 00:02:49.317
(crowd cheering)

00:02:53.223 --> 00:02:54.056
No!

00:02:55.493 --> 00:02:56.326
[Man In Crowd] Yeah!

00:02:56.326 --> 00:02:57.726
Who the (bleep) is that guy?

00:02:57.726 --> 00:02:59.201
(crowd laughing)

00:02:59.201 --> 00:03:03.358
♪ Skippy, Skippy ♪

00:03:03.358 --> 00:03:06.398
♪ Skippy (mumbles) true ♪

00:03:06.398 --> 00:03:07.231
(laughing)

00:03:07.231 --> 00:03:10.132
Wait a minute, you have
the lyrics right here.

00:03:10.132 --> 00:03:11.330
(crowd laughing)

00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:12.676
They're right here and you're like,

00:03:12.676 --> 00:03:14.076
Skippy, Skippy, va va va va.

00:03:15.095 --> 00:03:15.928
(crowd laughing)

00:03:15.928 --> 00:03:17.907
That's how Americans
sing The National Anthem.

00:03:17.907 --> 00:03:19.330
(crowd laughing)

00:03:19.330 --> 00:03:20.163
Skippy!

00:03:21.226 --> 00:03:23.107
Skippy oi oi!

00:03:23.107 --> 00:03:27.046
Oi Skippy (crowd laughing)
Skippy Bush Kangaroo!

00:03:27.046 --> 00:03:30.622
(crowd cheering and clapping)

00:03:30.622 --> 00:03:32.606
Thank you Sydney!

00:03:32.606 --> 00:03:33.785
Thank you Australia!

00:03:33.785 --> 00:03:37.618
(crowd cheering and clapping)

